# Enterprise AMS (PulsePoint)

When work touches **statewide association** structure, departments, advocacy, emergency, org hierarchy, or IT handoff:

## Canonical references

- Departments: `lib/association/departments.ts` (16 departments)
- Modules / phases: `lib/association/modules.ts`
- RBAC: `lib/permissions.ts` + `lib/association/rbac-matrix.ts`
- UI hub: `app/[orgSlug]/(admin)/enterprise/`
- Master prompt: `docs/ENTERPRISE-AMS-OPTIMIZED-PROMPT.md`
- Architecture: `docs/ENTERPRISE-ARCHITECTURE.md`
- Azure swap: `docs/ENTERPRISE-INTEGRATION.md`
- **Backups mandatory:** `docs/BACKUP-REQUIREMENTS.md` — run `pnpm continuity:backup` before schema migrations

## Rules

1. New persistent models → add to `lib/org-models.ts` + backup/export scripts
2. All data access via `getOrgDb(orgId)`; `requireCapability` on mutations
3. Phase labels: `live` | `alpha` | `foundation` | `roadmap` — no false GA claims
4. Do not invent healthcare statistics in advocacy/quality copy
5. Microsoft/Azure: adapter + env only until `INTEGRATION_PROFILE=hap-azure` approved

## Multi-agent split

| Agent | Owns |
|-------|------|
| Members/CRM | `MemberOrganization`, `MemberPulse`, committees |
| Advocacy | `AdvocacyIssue`, Engage campaigns |
| Emergency | `EmergencyContact`, readiness reports |
| Platform | RBAC, integrations, backups, audit |
| Data | `continuity:export`, warehouse field dictionary |
